  189 2766 ~            ; [HL] = [HL] * [DE]. The significands' product, 128 bits, by shift and add, a multiplier bit at a
  190 2766 ~            ; time from the bottom: qr is its top half, and each step adds the multiplicand to it if the bit
  191 2766 ~            ; is set and shifts it down a place, the carry of the addition in at the top. The top half is the
  192 2766 ~            ; result's significand -- shifted up a place when the leading one is at bit 126 rather than 127 --
  193 2766 ~            ; and what comes off its bottom only a sticky bit (qst), ORed into bit 0, which is below the round
  194 2766 ~            ; bit either way. Both significands have their lowest eleven bits zero (fifty-three bits at the
  195 2766 ~            ; top of sixty-four): the multiplier's lowest byte would only shift a zero qr, so the loop starts
  196 2766 ~            ; at its second, and the multiplicand's lowest byte adds nothing, so the addition starts at its
  197 2766 ~            ; second. The eight-byte addition and shift are written out, not called: three times as fast.
