 4582 285A ~                ; together in D behind a sentinel bit that drops out at the eighth step; from 2^23 it is
 4583 285A ~                ; thirty-two, DE:HL, and the quotient's byte waits in rt_lo. The divisor's low word is in BC,
 4584 285A ~                ; to add; the rest of it, and its negative to take it off, in memory -- -d in rt_r, which the
 4585 285A ~                ; remainder replaces at the end. As the 16-bit passes do, the carry tells which way the
 4586 285A ~                ; remainder went, which holds while the doubled remainder fits: hence the limits 2^23 and
 4587 285A ~                ; 2^31. From 2^31 the quotient is 0 or 1.
