 6146 2896 ~            ; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 6147 2896 ~            ; HL = destination, DE = source, BC = count. The same direction and the same
 6148 2896 ~            ; register convention as the reference generator's inline expansion, so that the
 6149 2896 ~            ; two back ends agree about what a struct assignment does.
 6150 2896 ~            ;
 6151 2896 ~            ; A count of zero copies nothing: the test is at the top, unlike the inline
 6152 2896 ~            ; version, because here the count can come from anywhere.
 6153 2896 ~            ; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
